The first ARPANET message was sent from UCLA (Leonard Kleinrock's lab, SDS Sigma 7) to the second node at SRI — the Stanford Research Institute in Menlo Park — where Bill Duvall was on an SDS 940. Charley Kline typed "LO" before the crash, then completed "LOGIN" after restart.

The proposed answer mislabels the receiving institution as "Stanford University," but SRI (Stanford Research Institute) had been a separate, independent organization since 1970... more importantly, in common usage and factually, SRI is not Stanford University. It also swaps the machines (UCLA had the Sigma 7; SRI had the 940). The correct institution is SRI / Stanford Research Institute.

