The proposed answer says seven, but this conflicts with the well-documented record: Michael Jackson won **eight** Grammy Awards at the 26th Annual Grammys, setting a record for most Grammys won in a single night.

The listed seven categories are accurate: Album of the Year (*Thriller*), Record of the Year ("Beat It"), Best Pop Vocal Performance Male (*Thriller*), Best Rock Vocal Performance Male ("Beat It"), Best R&B Vocal Performance Male ("Billie Jean"), Best R&B Song ("Billie Jean"), and Best Recording for Children (*E.T.*). The eighth award was **Producer of the Year (Non-Classical)**, which Jackson won jointly with Quincy Jones for *Thriller*. Since Jackson received the award alongside Jones (not merely "associated with" production), it counts in his personal tally, making his total eight, not seven.

