The proposed answer contains a plausible-sounding but incorrect claim. While Hegel did indeed complete the manuscript in Jena in October 1806 (with the famous anecdote about finishing the last pages as Napoleon's troops entered the city), the book was actually **published in 1807**. It was printed in Bamberg and Würzburg by Joseph Anton Goebert, and it appeared in early April 1807 (with the title page bearing the date 1807). The completion of the manuscript and the publication date are different things — Hegel sent corrections to the publisher even after leaving Jena, and the finished book only appeared in 1807.

Therefore, the proposed answer of 1806 is wrong.

